BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventriversandrails3amarathonhalfmarathon5k26289-20261114@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261113T173759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
SUMMARY:Rivers and Rails: Marathon\, Half-Marathon\, 5K
DESCRIPTION:Join us on November 14\, 2026 for the Rivers and Rails Marathon Weekend in historic Brunswick\, Maryland. This event features a full marathon\, a half marathon\, and the Veterans Challenge 5K. Runners experience scenic river crossings over both the Potomac and Shenandoah Rivers\, along with views of historic rail corridors and the natural beauty of the C and O Canal Towpath. The full marathon takes participants through Brunswick\, Harpers Ferry\, and Bolivar\, offering a memorable journey through three unique communities. Professional chip timing\, aid stations\, commemorative shirts\, and custom finisher medals are provided for all registered runners. The Veterans Challenge 5K remains entirely within Brunswick and honors service members with a challenging and meaningful course that passes several veterans memorials. All races begin near the entrance to the C&O Canal Towpath in Brunswick\, and no course crosses railroad tracks.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/rivers-and-rails%3a-marathon-half-marathon-5k/26289/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsweaterweatherindowntownfrederick26336-20261114@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261113T173759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
SUMMARY:Sweater Weather in Downtown Frederick
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for the coziest time of year: SWEATER WEATHER! On Saturday\, November 14\, slip into your coziest sweater and shop local! You’ll be given a raffle ticket and entered to win Downtown Frederick Partnership gift cards for every $20 you spend at two dozen of your favorite local businesses! Several participating businesses will offer additional specials\, discounts\, or freebies to customers wearing sweaters\, so come get cozy in Downtown Frederick!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/sweater-weather-in-downtown-frederick/26336/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsweetdreams3amandybarnettsingspatsycline25957-20261114@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261113T173759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
SUMMARY:Sweet Dreams: Mandy Barnett Sings Patsy Cline
DESCRIPTION:“Sweet Dreams” is a stunning tribute to the timeless music of Patsy Cline. The concert features a collection of iconic classic country songs originally recorded by Patsy Cline\, including “Crazy\,” “Sweet Dreams\,” “Walking After Midnight\,” “I Fall to Pieces\,” “Always\,” “Faded Love\,” “She’s Got You\,” “Strange\,” and many more. Widely considered Nashville’s finest vocalist\, Mandy Barnett rose to prominence at the age of 18 after being chosen among 400 auditionees by the legendary Ryman Auditorium for the title role in the 1994 musical production of Always… Patsy Cline . Her successful performance as Patsy Cline garnered tremendous press\, both domestic and international\, establishing the production as a staple of American theater. An official member of the Grand Ole Opry since 2021\, Mandy has performed on more than 400 occasions\, sharing the stage with legendary performers including Dolly Parton\, Ringo Starr\, Kristin Chenoweth\, Pat Benatar\, Judy Collins\, Connie Stevens\, Garth Brooks\, and Michael Feinstein\, among numerous others. Learn more about “Sweet Dreams” and Mandy Barnett by visiting her official website. This show is part of the Weinberg Center’s Centennial Events\, celebrating 100 years of entertainment in our historic building. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop and timeless atmosphere for a meaningful entertainment experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/sweet-dreams%3a-mandy-barnett-sings-patsy-cline/25957/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtheaddamsfamilymusical26251-20261114@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261113T173759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
SUMMARY:The Addams Family Musical
DESCRIPTION:The students from Dance Unlimited’s fall musical theatre workshop are proud to present The Addams Family! This 60 minute musical tells the story of Wednesday Addams who has fallen in love with a sweet\, “normal” young man from a respectable family. When the two families meet for dinner\, the Addams family’s strange and silly world is turned upside down. Join us in our 115-seat theatre and enjoy a family friendly performance from our talented students! Please call for assistance with reserved Handicapped Seating.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-addams-family-musical/26251/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventyourbodyinyoga3aafunctionalanatomyweekendwithmachellelee26311-20261114@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261113T173759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:YOUR Body in Yoga: A Functional Anatomy Weekend with Machelle Lee
DESCRIPTION:Harshly judging one's range of motion is one of the greatest sources of unnecessary suffering in many people’s yoga practice. The poses in yoga are intended to be a method to move the regenerative and healing life force. To do that effectively in yoga\, we must understand each of our own (or our students) unique structures and explore when we can move more deeply into a posture or when to acknowledge limitations with respect. Although some restrictions in range of motion are related to tight muscles\, and more are related to contracted fascia and ligaments\, many significant limitations are actually due to variations in bone shapes and joint orientations that can differ dramatically from one person to the next. Understanding YOUR yoga anatomy is best learned through direct hands-on experience - testing your bones/joints and witnessing them curiously and compassionately to the bones of others. This functional\, comparative anatomy workshop explores the 14 major joint segments of the body that account for most of our yoga postures. For each joint intersection\, we will perform bone analysis and range of motion tests on ourselves\, compare with each other\, and demonstrate how each varying joints will express itself in specific yoga postures. 12 CEUs Available for Yoga Teachers with Yoga Alliance Anatomy is a vast subject\, but this interactive workshop reveals the basics in a way that clarifies and simplifies the yoga practice - putting the attention back where it belongs - how the key action of each pose makes you FEEL and moves the life force. In this workshop\, participants often experience an “ah-ha” moment about their body and their practice\, which can be powerfully liberating and self-accepting. This workshop is ideal for all yoga practitioners\, whether one is a beginner or experienced student wishing to deepen their knowledge of their body in practice and for yoga teachers looking to expand their teaching and cueing.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/your-body-in-yoga%3a-a-functional-anatomy-weekend-with-machelle-lee/26311/
END:VEVENT
